---
// QR target for DTRUE 2026 (D46): https://nanjierao.github.io/demos/csudt/
// Links the two self-contained demo files in public/demos/csudt/, which are not modified here.
// S4 turns this into the full explainer.
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CS-UDT demo"
  description="CS-UDT, a crowd-sourced urban digital twin for hurricane flooding in Jacksonville: a planner dashboard and a zero-install citizen client, running on simulated data."
>
  <p class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/research/civic-digital-twins/">Civic digital twins</a>
  </p>
  <h1>CS-UDT flood digital twin</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lede">
      A crowd-sourced urban digital twin for hurricane flooding in Jacksonville. Everything in the
      demo is simulated: the replay is modeled on Hurricane Irma (Sep 10–12, 2017), and the
      community content is synthetic.
    </p>

    <ul class="demo-links plain-list">
      <li>
        <a class="button button--primary" href="/demos/csudt/csudt_dashboard.html">
          Planner dashboard
        </a>
        <p class="small">
          The twin’s map view. Press Play to run the simulated replay and watch reports converge
          into confirmed events. Best on a large screen.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="button" href="/demos/csudt/csudt_mobile.html">
          Citizen client
        </a>
        <p class="small">
          The zero-install client residents would use: report, take quests, verify. Best on a phone.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What the demo loads and asks for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The dashboard loads MapLibre GL JS from unpkg.com and map tiles from OpenStreetMap (©
        OpenStreetMap contributors).
      </li>
      <li>The citizen client loads qrcode.js from cdnjs.cloudflare.com.</li>
      <li>
        The citizen client can ask for your location and motion sensors, only when you tap the
        button that uses them. Your demo reports stay in your browser (localStorage); the demo sends
        nothing to this site.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Background:{' '}
      <a href="/research/civic-digital-twins/">Civic AI: crowd-sourced urban digital twins</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/builds/cs-udt/">CS-UDT build</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .demo-links li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .demo-links p {
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 0;
  }
</style>
